<title>INDIA: General Motors chief postpones India visit.</title>
<headline>General Motors chief postpones India visit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp chairman John Smith has postponed a planned visit to India this month because of labour negotiations in North America, company officials said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said a strike and labour negotiations had forced Smith to postpone the visit, which had been planned for October 15. No date was set for a rescheduled visit.</p>
<p>The U.S. car maker has a joint venture to produce cars with India's Hindustan Motors Ltd.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
